      "descripcioPlatja": "It is part of the series of beaches that were recovered along the coastline of Barcelona as part of the urban renovation that took place for the Barcelona Olympic Games. It sits between two breakwaters: one that separates it from Llevant Beach to the northeast, and another, the Bac de Roda breakwater, which separates it from La Mar Bella Beach to the southwest. ",
      "playascercanas": [
        {
          "id": 152,
          "nombre": "de Llevant",
          "costaid": 2,
          "descripcion": "It is the last beach of those created along the Barcelona coastline, and was introduced to the city in the summer of 2006. The beach is bounded by a breakwater (which separates it from the site of the future marine zoo) to the northeast and by another breakwater to the southwest, which separates it from La Nova Mar Bella Beach. ",
          "distancia": 0.4,
          "favorita": false,
          "imagen_url": "B39405_Barcelona_Llevant_general.jpg",
          "costa": "Costa Barcelona Nord"
        },
        {
          "id": 154,
          "nombre": "La Mar Bella Beach ",
          "costaid": 2,
          "descripcion": "This is one of the beaches that were created as part of the urban remodelling of the coastline that took place in 1992 for the Barcelona Olympic Games. It sits between two breakwaters: the Bac de Roda breakwater to the northeast, which separates it from La Nova Mar Bella Beach; and the El Ferrocarril breakwater to the southwest, which separates it from Bogatell Beach. ",
          "distancia": 0.45,
          "favorita": false,
          "imagen_url": "B39605_Barcelona_MarBella_general.jpg",
          "costa": "Costa Barcelona Nord"
        },
        {
          "id": 155,
          "nombre": "Bogatell Beach ",
          "costaid": 2,
          "descripcion": "This is one of the beaches that acquired a new status when the remodelling of the Barcelona coastline took place during the nineties. It sits between two breakwaters: the El Ferrocarril breakwater to the northeast, which separates it from La Mar Bella Beach; and the Bogatell breakwater to the southwest, which separates it from La Nova Icària Beach. ",
          "distancia": 1.15,
          "favorita": false,
          "imagen_url": "B39705_Barcelona_Bogatell_general.jpg",
          "costa": "Costa Barcelona Nord"
        }
